cd folder

Command 1: Compile the C file
arm-none-eabi-gcc -mcpu=cortex-m3 -mthumb -O0 -g -c add_prog.c -o add_prog.o

Command 2: Assemble the startup file
arm-none-eabi-as -mcpu=cortex-m3 -mthumb startup_stm32f103.s -o startup.o

Command 3: Link the object files
arm-none-eabi-ld -T STM32F103C8.ld add_prog.o startup.o -o firmware.elf

Command 4: Convert ELF into binary
arm-none-eabi-objcopy -O binary firmware.elf firmware.bin

Step 3 - Flash the firmware onto the Blue Pill
st-flash write firmware.bin 0x08000000


5. Step 4 — Start the debugging server
Open Terminal 1 and run:
st-util

Now open Terminal 2 in the same project folder.
Start GDB:
gdb-multiarch firmware.elf

Step 5 — Execute these commands inside GDB
Once you see the (gdb) prompt, enter the following commands one at a time.
A. Connect to the board
target extended-remote :4242

set disassemble-next-line on
display/i $pc
display $sp
display/x $r7
display/8xw $sp
display/x $lr